{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And if YHWH your Elohim enlarges your border.</b> This passage is a promise for the future, and it is what was said to Abraham in the Covenant Between the Pieces (Genesis 15): ״לזרעך נתתי את הארץ הזאת מנהר מצרים עד הנהר הגדול נהר פרת״ — 'To your seed I have given this land, from the river of Egypt to the great river, the river Euphrates.' And there it goes on to enumerate ten nations; seven of them were conquered in the days of Joshua, and three remained — Kenite, Kenizzite, and Kadmonite — which were never conquered, but are for the future. And the word ואם 'and if' is in the language of certainty, and what indicates this is what it says, ״כאשר נשבע״ — 'as He swore' — that is, there is an oath in this matter. And like it (Exodus 20:22): ״ואם מזבח אבנים תעשה לי״, which is in the language of certainty; and so too (Exodus 22:24): ״אם כסף תלוה״; and so too (Leviticus 2:14): ״ואם תקריב מנחת בכורים״ — for behold, we find them in the Torah elsewhere as independent commandments, and this demonstrates that the word אם is in the language of certainty."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Citations follow the verse numbering given in the source; (שמות כ) refers to Exodus 20:22 in standard enumeration (Altar of stones, v. 22 in some editions; here rendered as cited). The abbreviation ל,י in the Exodus quotation resolved as לי."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:28.085461696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}